    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass and the build succeeds. Let me verify my E.164 logic handles the spec's edge cases correctly with a quick reasoning check against the three tests plus the duplicate-detection requirement:\n\n- `coreNationalToE164`: `\"0412 345 678\"` \u2192 strip spaces \u2192 `0412345678` \u2192 drop leading `0` \u2192 `412345678` \u2192 prepend `61` \u2192 `+61412345678` \u2713\n- `functionalityKeepsExplicitCountryCode`: `\"+64 21 123 456\"` \u2192 `+6421123456` \u2192 keep `+` and country code \u2192 `+6421123456` \u2713\n- `errorRejectsUnformattable`: `\"12\"` \u2192 `+6112` \u2192 only 4 digits (< 8) \u2192 rejected as 400 \u2713\n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Behavior change: telephone stored/compared as E.164**\n\n1. **`TelephoneE164.java`** (new) \u2014 shared normalizer: strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+` and its country code when present, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, returning `null` (\u2192 invalid) otherwise.\n\n2. **`ValidateOwnerFields.java`** \u2014 `normalizeTelephone` now converts to E.164 and stores it back on the request; an unformattable number adds a `telephone` error \u2192 **400** (replaces the old strip-to-10-digits rule).\n\n3. **`CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique.java`** \u2014 duplicate detection now compares **E.164** values (both request and each existing owner normalized via `TelephoneE164`), replacing the old raw-digit comparison.\n\n4. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 entity constraint changed from `@Digits`/10-digit `@Pattern` to `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` so the persisted E.164 value validates; removed the now-unused `@Digits` import.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `telephone` description, example (`+61412345678`), and input pattern to reflect E.164 storage.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.",
